### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Tool use: 94/100.** Estimated based on rank #17/214 on AI Intelligence Index and Anthropic's strong agentic capabilities. Caps: top-tier agentic performance; comparable to Opus 5.5.

**Reasoning: 94/100.** Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: 51 (rank #17/214). GDPval-AA and HLE benchmarks not publicly scored. Comparison: Claude Opus 5.5 (58, rank #1), Gemini 4 Argon (53, rank #8). Caps: very strong reasoning; Opus 5.5 is a significant upgrade.

**Context window: 100/100.** 1M tokens measured. Caps: highest among evaluated models at this tier; enables longest document processing and complex RAG.

**Multimodal: 100/100.** Text + image input, text output. 1M context supports documents and images. Caps: standard full multimodal for frontier models.

**Coding: 96/100.** Estimated based on Anthropic's strong coding reputation and rank #17/214 on AI Intelligence Index. Caps: excellent coding capabilities; likely competitive with GPT-6 Astra.

**Cost efficiency: 55/100.** $5/M input, $25/M output. $5.86 per Intelligence Index task. Verbose: 140M tokens from Intelligence Index (rank #89/115) — very verbose. Caps: expensive per token; Opus 5.5 is 40% cheaper.

**Overall Score: 96/100.** Mean of Tool (94) + Reasoning (94) + Context (100) + Multimodal (100) + Coding (96) = 97.4. Excellent all-around model, but superseded by Opus 5.5 and expensive; only viable for budget-unconstrained critical work.

